# hyprconf — Keychron / Lemokey HID access for the web-based launcher.
#
# TAG+="uaccess" is the whole mechanism: systemd's 73-seat-late.rules turns the
# tag into a POSIX ACL (user:<active-seat-user>:rw-) on the hidraw node, which
# is what lets launcher.keychron.com reach a board over WebHID without running
# the browser as root. That rule matches on TAG==, so this file MUST sort
# before it — hence 70-, not 99-.
#
# No MODE=: it would set 0660 root:root and grant a desktop user nothing. The
# ACL is what grants access (/dev/uinput on a stock Arch box is uaccess-tagged
# with no MODE= and no GROUP=, and lands at 0600 root:root plus that ACL).
#
# Vendor-only matches on purpose. The vendor-defined interface the launcher
# talks to is not in a fixed place: if01 on a Q2 Max, if03 on a Link dongle,
# usage page 0xFF0A on a 4K Link where the others use 0xFF60 — and two dongles
# sharing a product id can expose different interface counts depending on
# pairing state. The vendor id is the only stable thing, and it also covers the
# mice behind the 2.4GHz receivers.
#
# Bluetooth-paired boards are NOT covered: their hidraw parent is a Bluetooth
# device with no idVendor attribute. A KERNELS=="*3434:*" line would reach them.
#
# Undo: README › Reverting to stock.
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3434", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="362d", TAG+="uaccess"
